    "body": "### Checklist\n\n- [x] I have searched for a similar issue in this repository and did not find one.\n- [x] I am using an official build obtained from [releases](https://github.com/shadps4-emu/shadPS4/releases) or updated one of those builds using its in-app updater.\n\n### Describe the Bug\n\nThe D-Pad when using an external controller or the controller on my Ayn Odin 3 is stuck on 2 axis, and can only be mapped to two of the 4 directions, and even then it won't work. The automap feature doesn't help, and maps the D-Pad to another series of unknown buttons. No idea how to fix this or what's causing it\nDevice: Ayn Odin 3\n\n### Reproduction Steps\n\nGo to controller in settings and try and map the D-Pad to a controller, my odin 3 controls are spoofed as an Xbox controller.\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nI just wanna know how to fix this or if there is a way to fix the D-Pad, bloodborne needs it\n\n### Specify OS Version\n\nAndroid\n\n### CPU\n\nSnapdragon 8 Elite\n\n### GPU\n\nAdreno 830\n\n### Amount of RAM in GB\n\n12 GB",
